Fix compiling a quantifier that Dafny rewrites to break a matching loop, such as `if j, i :| 0 <= j < 5 && 0 <= i < (j - 1) * (j - 1) + 1 && i * j == 2`: the code referred to an undefined variable, and a C# assembly's Dafny source, which Dafny reads when the assembly is used as a library, did not parse; the verifier also no longer reports well-formedness errors that such a binding guard rules out, such as a division by zero
